t answers what the packet asked, all within its six allowed files and under the 800-line budget.\n\n**Goal:** `baseline.md` now has a section on Common's share of DocService CPU. It gives Common's own time, Common plus what it calls, the extra cost of the libraries only Common uses, and a \"% of wall\" figure. It covers co-edit load (50 docs × 5 clients) and ConvertService, at both WARN and DEBUG logging. It breaks the cost down for each area the packet named: tenant config lookups (`operationContext`), storage-base, the RabbitMQ task queue, `utils` and `logger`. It ends with a clear finding for DIAG-common: keep, because Common is about 1% of DocService's time under load.\n\n**The executor's departures are justified and written down:**\n- **Profiled from source:** the installed `docservice` binary ignores `NODE_OPTIONS`. The source run matched PKT-0018's co-edit latency, so it is representative.\n- **Windowed profiling instead of plain `--cpu-prof`:** plain `--cpu-prof` captures mostly startup and only writes on a clean exit. An idle 12 s profile showed 48% \"Common\" just from loading modules, which shows the change was needed.\n- **`convert-large.js` instead of `e2e-convert.js`:** the latter sends no JWT and this install requires one.\n\n**Measurement honesty:**\n- **Wall time:** the CPU profile can't attribute wall time per request. The section says so and defines \"% of wall\" as Common's CPU over the profiled window.\n- **Logging level:** the VM had been left at DEBUG. The executor measured both levels instead of quietly mixing them.\n\n**Attribution script (`profile-common.js`):** the method looks correct.\n- Common's own time is counted when the innermost frame is in Common.\n- \"Inclusive\" time is counted when any frame on the stack is in Common.\n- The \"+ libs\" figure covers libraries whose async callbacks run with no Common frame on the stack, and the section explains why.\n- The function that brings the cost into Common is taken from the outermost Common frame on the stack. That is the right choice.\n\n**Process checks:**\n- The Executor log is filled in.\n- No follow-ups were requested; the log explicitly says none were spawned.\n- This is an investigation packet, so the rule about keeping surprising behavior in a test doesn't apply.\n- The contract holds: no tests or source files were touched.\n- The friction line is appended.\n\n**Minor issues, not blocking:**\n- The header comment in `profile-common.js` still says the profile comes from `node --cpu-prof`. In practice it came from `profile-toggle.js`.\n- At DEBUG, ConvertService shows lower DocService CPU (0.037 cores) than at WARN (0.043). That is probably run-to-run noise and doesn't affect the finding.\n- The raw profiles are only in `/tmp/prof` and weren't committed, which is acceptable given their size.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Common's share measured and recorded in baseline.md with sound method, documented deviations, and a clear keep finding.","ttft_ms":1964,"type":"result","duration_ms":16061,"uuid":"dcd0423c-fab4-446b-861a-f17b1f0ddc8e","ttft_stream_ms":824,"time_to_request_ms":331,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":203,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":2,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":46,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":171,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":228,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":254,"process_cpu_ms_turn":909,"process_wall_ms_turn":16061,"process_cpu_ms_streamin